<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Carthaginian Iberia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">237–206 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Carthaginian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a> was the territory in southern and eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> ruled by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a> under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcid-family">Barcid family</a> from 237 BCE, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamilcar-barca">Hamilcar Barca</a> landed at Gades, until the Roman conquest in 206 BCE. Its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> mines and manpower rebuilt Carthaginian power after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-punic-war">First Punic War</a>, its capital was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthago-nova">Carthago Nova</a>, and it was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal">Hannibal</a>'s base for the invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> in 218 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/carthaginian-iberia.jpg" alt="Carthaginian Iberia" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dama_de_Elche_(M.A.N._Madrid)_04.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
